From 1e17efbaf511d6611246b948969e711e42329db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:08:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stream camera bands without blocking field ticks

Preflight the incoming background band and read missing tiles through the existing asynchronous ring while field logic and animation continue. Protect incoming tiles until the complete band has been uploaded. Use the loaded window margin during reads and retain excess scroll for gradual catch-up, including after pad release. Forced map uploads and the battle camera keep their existing paths.

Express the original camera-band intervals arithmetically, preserving their gaps and inclusive endpoints. An independent host comparison against the preceding implementation passes 8,690,592 cases including upload events. This recovers the space required by the asynchronous camera path: on the same eight-language layout main_BSS_END moves from 0x801ceb00 to 0x801ceab4, recovering 80 bytes of aligned heap.
